// @emit-error call to unknown function
// The checker declares ten memory intrinsics; the emitter lowers three
// (`__store_i32__`, `__load_i32__`, `__log__`). The other seven — this one
// included — pass `vl check` clean and then fail at EMIT, so the split is a
// real part of the contract and is pinned here rather than left to be
// rediscovered. The diagnostic reads like a typo'd identifier, which is the
// half worth fixing first (`docs/internals/buffer-design.md` §B1).
__store_f32__(0, 1.5 as f32)
print(__load_i32__(0))
